Z||000000||beachbomb||06-21-2001||05:08 PM||||Hey all, is it possible to get the recall parts for my '84 4 cyclinder, i have an extra engine that has had no recalls done on it and i would like to do the recalls on it when i remove the engine from my spare Indy.<BR>Any help here is greatly appreciated, like parts #'s, where to get it, does it come in one big package deal or a bunch of little parts. I called my local Pontiac dealer today and he said i would 1: have to drive the car in to get this done(car is not in drivable state), and 2) i would have to supply the recall paperwork because he had to idea or clue about a Fiero recall...thanks..Jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||06-21-2001||06:00 PM||||Hit the cave link below. What you need to know is in there.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-21-2001||08:21 PM||||You may be able to order the part kit in recall 89V232000 (88-C-23A) but you will pay for it. Recall work will only be done to a whole car. (The recalls apply to parts other than the engine block.)<P>In you're case... you need to read the 87V181000 (84-C-15B) recall very carefully. It explains all the problems to look for with the 84 block.||||reg||1
